               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 69-year-old male patient, admitted on 08/07/2012 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, pulse oximetry, and blood tests, confirming an acute exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids. Clinical condition improved satisfactorily. He is discharged in stable condition and we recommend continuation of his inhaled maintenance therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Pulmonary rehabilitation is advised. Please do not hesitate to contact us for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
